# | Moxa ioThinx 45MR-7210 — System Power + Field Power Input Monitor
# | 
# | Source: ioThinx 4510 Series User's Manual V2.1, August 2019, Appendix A
# | Protocol: Modbus/TCP via ioThinx 4510 adapter, port 502
# | 
# | IMPORTANT: Addresses are MODULE-RELATIVE. Actual PDU address = slot_base + relative_address.
# | Slot base depends on which slot this module occupies in the ioThinx 4510 chassis.
# | 
# | Monitors system power (SP) and field power (FP) rails.
# | spLowerLimitValue and spUpperLimitValue define the alarm threshold window for system power.
# | 
# | FC03 (holding R/W): see [[registers]] below
# | (No FC01/FC02/FC04 entries documented for this module)
@mbmap=1
@vendor=Moxa
@model=ioThinx 45MR-7210
@vendor_website=moxa.com
@description=System + field power input monitor ioThinx 45MR slot module. Addresses are module-relative; actual PDU address = slot_base + relative_address. FC03: spStatus (rel 0, system power status WORD), spLowerLimitValue (rel 1-2, f32 lower alarm threshold), spUpperLimitValue (rel 3-4, f32 upper alarm threshold), fpStatus (rel 5, field power status WORD). Write spLowerLimitValue/spUpperLimitValue to configure system power alarm thresholds.
@source=Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST), modbus-library/moxa-iothinx-45mr-7210.toml; Source: ioThinx 4510 Series User's Manual V2.1, August 2019, Appendix A. Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation
